From 60eb4406a8b42d7985e9c2a70ac4aabb6f38257a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Reed <reedswork@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:02:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] QPACK codec reachable for a client that writes its own
 streams

stomp-h3's WebTransport session drives its QUIC connection itself
(Chrome's control stream, extended CONNECT and capsules, byte for byte)
instead of through h3's client, which refuses streams the server opens
and orders its writes its own way. It still needs QPACK: the response
to its CONNECT may use the server's dynamic table, which the decoder of
patch 0003 handles, and its request fields are Huffman coded where that
is shorter, as Chrome's are.

A hidden module, qpack_codec, exposes that decoder (encoder stream in,
Insert Count Increment and Section Acknowledgment out, blocked sections
detected by their Required Insert Count), the static table lookups and
the Huffman encoder. Nothing else in h3 changes.
